{
  "_comment": [
    "Car wraps (tools/make-car-wraps.js reads this; run it, then tools/build-pack.js).",
    "geometries: one voxel model per car shape. model = the MTVehicles model with the elements; atlas = the plain color whose trim",
    "(tires, glass, lights, interior; pick one with plain rims) the wrapped car keeps; compare = plain colors of the same shape: a",
    "pixel with each color's body color in most of them is paint; decals = colors in the atlas (white racing stripes) that the wrap",
    "covers where they touch the paint (only listed colors: seats can look like stripes to the comparison). front = the model axis",
    "the car's nose points to (display.head turns the model: +90 = +x, -90 = -x).",
    "family = the MTVehicles family in vehicles.yml the wrap variants go into; label names the variants (\"Wrap Sedan Camo\"); price",
    "is MTVehicles' own (unused by Donating).",
    "cars: Donating's car ids (core.sk) -> their geometry. carwraps.sk gets {-carwrap::<car>::<wrap>} for each.",
    "families: families this script adds to vehicles.yml (plain colors with MTVehicles' default uuids and itemDamages, and the",
    "extra colors MTVehicles' pack draws but its default vehicles.yml doesn't list: those get a new damage and uuid).",
    "wraps: id, name, tier (common = bad, rare = good, exotic = super rare), glow (full-bright paint), frames / frametime",
    "(animated), and the pattern's parameters (colors are RGB).",
    "Once cars with a wrap exist, never rename or remove that wrap or change a geometry's label or family: the variant",
    "\"Wrap <label> <name>\" would get a new itemDamage and uuid (or leave vehicles.yml), and the cars of the old one lose their",
    "model. Retire a wrap in core.sk instead (carwrap::<id>::retired); its pattern and colors can still change."
  ],
